--   **The moved records are few.**
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.R6IL2CCount`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.IL2C.Lay.card_moved_C (h : l.OK) (hQC : l.QC = Qc G n) (hQL : l.QL = 2 ^ L) (hK : 1 ≤ K)
--       (hG : 1 ≤ G) (hL : ρ + n * K ≤ L) :
--       nMv (l.stepP (fun x c => TlS K ρ n x (Psi K ρ G n L x c))) l.M * (2 ^ G * 2 ^ K) ≤
--         n * l.M * (2 * 2 ^ K + (2 * 2 ^ G + 2) * 2 ^ G)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Round six, compact controls (I2C): the moved records are few
--
--   The correction key `κ = stepP (TlS ∘ Psi)` fixes every record whose state is `Good`
--   (`Psi_good`, `Tl_Tl`). A record is not good only if one of the `n` digits of `T` or `U` is
--   `2^G - 1`, or one of the `n` guard segments of `Y` is out of range (`2·2^G + 2` values of
--   `2^K`).
--
--   **`card_moved_C`**: `#{m < M : κ m ≠ m} · 2^G · 2^K ≤ n · M · (2 · 2^K + (2 · 2^G + 2) · 2^G)`.
